// TEST: unknown-reason opaque builtin result
// TEST: native-gap "string_trim is an opaque total function, an accepted model choice (ADR-2026-10-08-1422): a string with nothing to trim is not shown to be a run, so native stays unknown where ESBMC refutes it with an unconstrained result" #1890
// `string_trim` never grows a string (a fact the model keeps), but whether it shortens one depends
// on the Unicode white space the model does not encode: a counterexample "a string with nothing to
// trim" is the result of the call being as long as its operand, which the opaque result allows and
// the real call also gives, but the verifier cannot tell which, so it is unknown.
module TrimShortensOpaque

fn trimmed_is_shorter(s: String) -> bool vow {
  ensures: result == true
} {
  string_trim(s).len() < s.len()
}

fn main() -> i32 [io] {
  if trimmed_is_shorter(String::from(" a ")) { 0 } else { 1 }
}
